{"id":"building-inspections","title":"Federal inspection scores of subsidised buildings","question":"Which federally subsidised apartment buildings in San Francisco scored worst when federal inspectors last walked through, and who owns and manages them?","finding":"Of 119 subsidised buildings inspected since 2022, 3 scored under 60 out of 100, the federal failing line, and 5 fell 15 points or more from their previous inspection; the middle score is 92. The lowest is Plaza (1230 Eddy St) at 29 on 2025-04-01, down from 82 in 2017. When the Housing Authority's own estates were last scored (2013–2017), 11 of 27 were under 60.","how":"Latest score for each building in the U.S. housing department's inspection files (nine releases, 2015 to November 2026), with the score before it. Owner and manager are the organizations named in the department's list of buildings with rent-subsidy contracts. Only buildings inspected since January 2022 are ranked; the same inspection listed twice under different dates is counted once.","limits":"A score reflects one visit, and the federal scoring method changed in 2023, so a fall across that change is not a like-for-like comparison. Old buildings housing very poor tenants score lower for reasons an owner may not control. The files list an owner company for each building, often a single-building partnership; matching it to a City-paid organization is by name only. Public-housing estates left the inspection files as they were converted to private management.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"building","t":"Building","type":"text"},{"k":"programme","t":"Kind","type":"text"},{"k":"homes","t":"Homes","type":"int"},{"k":"owner","t":"Owner on file","type":"text"},{"k":"manager","t":"Manager on file","type":"text"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City-paid organization (name match)","type":"org"},{"k":"score","t":"Latest score","type":"int"},{"k":"date","t":"Date","type":"date"},{"k":"previous","t":"Score before","type":"int"},{"k":"previousDate","t":"Date"